@@ -0,0 +1,19 @@
+<h2>The originate certification verify route refuses a caller who is not a party, as GET /:id does &mdash; KS-1699 (verify only)</h2>
+<div class="note"><table class="pmatrix"><tr><td class="pm-topic" rowspan="2"><strong>What to know.</strong></td><td> <code>POST /api/certifications/:id/verify</code> in <code>services/originate</code> used to answer any authenticated same-tenant caller with <code>status</code>, <code>checks</code>, the issuer's <code>id</code> and <code>did</code> and the raw <code>blockchain</code> object, and to write a <code>verification</code> charge event for them. It now answers only a platform admin, the issuer, the holder and the issuing connector. Anyone else gets the route's own unknown-id answer (404, <code>{"verified":false,"error":"Certification not found"}</code>) and no charge event.
+    </td></tr><tr><td><strong>Audience narrowed, verify only.</strong> Whether verify, share and recertify should be open to a third-party verifier is an open question on KS-1699 for the owner to rule; <code>/:id/share</code> and <code>/:id/recertify</code> are unchanged here and the ticket stays open.
+    </td></tr></table>
+</div>
+<div class="note"><table class="pmatrix"><tr><td class="pm-topic" rowspan="1"><strong>Not measured here.</strong></td><td> No real gateway and originate pair, no real database, no Schemathesis or Akto run, no deploy.
+    </td></tr></table>
+</div>
+<h3>Checking it</h3>
