+<h2><!--n-->. The originate certification verify route refuses a caller who is not a party, as GET /:id does (KS-1699, verify only)</h2>
+<table class="pmatrix"><tr><td class="pm-topic" rowspan="2"><strong>What this changes.</strong></td><td> One handler, <code>POST /api/certifications/:id/verify</code> in <code>services/originate/src/routes/certifications.ts</code>. It looked a certification up by id and answered <code>status</code>, <code>checks</code>, <code>issuer {id, did}</code> and the raw <code>blockchain</code> object to any authenticated same-tenant caller, and wrote a <code>verification</code> charge event for that caller. It now applies <code>callerMayReadCertification</code>, the rule <code>GET /:id</code> already applies, after the not-found check and before the charge write.
+    </td></tr><tr><td><strong>A refused caller gets the route's own unknown-id answer.</strong> Same 404 status and the same bytes, <code>{"verified":false,"error":"Certification not found"}</code>, so "not yours" cannot be told from "no such certification", and no charge event is written. <strong>This narrows the audience</strong> to a platform admin, the issuer, the holder and the issuing connector; whether verify, share and recertify should be open to a third-party verifier is an open question on KS-1699 for the owner to rule. <strong>This is the verify route ONLY:</strong> <code>/:id/share</code> and <code>/:id/recertify</code> are untouched and the ticket stays open.
+    </td></tr></table>
+<h3><!--n-->.1 What proves it</h3>
+<table class="pmatrix"><tr><td class="pm-topic" rowspan="2"><strong>Red first, then green, then three plants.</strong></td><td> The new file <code>ks1699-certification-verify-needs-issuer-holder-or-admin.test.ts</code> has 23 cells. Over the unchanged route 12 fail and 11 pass; with the guard all 23 pass. Plant (a), the guard removed: 12 fail. Plant (b), the guard moved after the charge write: 3 fail (R2, R3, R5, each of which asserts no charge on the refused path). Plant (c), the guard inverted: 20 fail, only C1, C2 and C6 stay green.
+    </td></tr><tr><td><strong>The product change is 13 added lines and no changed or removed line</strong>: the guard (7 lines) and its comment (6 lines). The whole <code>services/originate</code> jest suite reads 222 files and 2,609 tests before and 223 files and 2,632 tests after, 0 failed on both sides, three interleaved pairs each.
+    </td></tr></table>
+<h3><!--n-->.2 What it does not cover</h3>
+<table class="pmatrix"><tr><td class="pm-topic" rowspan="1"><strong>Not measured here.</strong></td><td> No real gateway and originate pair, no real database (the cells use an in-process server and a mocked repository that honours the tenant), no Schemathesis or Akto run, and no deploy. Callers of the route outside this repository are not enumerated by this change.
+    </td></tr></table>
